{
  "title": "SRE-1803: backend services private behind the KrakenD gateway",
  "description": "Step-by-step verification of SRE-1803 (one group per stage of the ticket). Production is measured from Istio mesh metrics, gateway logs and RUM; SIT and UAT keep the curl checks on the ticket, RUM excepted.",
  "layout_type": "ordered",
  "reflow_type": "auto",
  "template_variables": [],
  "widgets": [
    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "**SRE-1803: make all backend services private, KrakenD as the only public API gateway.** One group per stage of the ticket, in the ticket's order. Each widget says which step it proves and what \"done\" looks like.\n\n**What Datadog can and cannot see.** Istio mesh metrics and application logs exist only for the production clusters (`prod-bravo-cluster`, `bfi-project-prod`). SIT and UAT are not monitored by Datadog, with one exception: RUM covers the consoles in every environment (`\u2026 Platform Test` applications). So production steps are measured here; the SIT and UAT steps keep the curl checks written on the ticket, repeated in the grey notes below.\n\nSources: the request counter `istio.mesh.request.count.total` (reporter: destination), the gateway's own logs (`service:prod-ms-krakend-gateway`, plugins `server-observer` and `server-realtime-proxy`), and RUM resource events. Ticket: [SRE-1803](https://bfifinance.atlassian.net/browse/SRE-1803). Programme page: [Make all backend services private behind gateway](https://bfifinance.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EA/pages/2819948675).",
        "background_color": "white",
        "font_size": "14",
        "text_align": "left",
        "has_padding": true,
        "show_tick": false
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "group",
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "show_title": true,
        "title": "Overall: how much production traffic still bypasses the gateway",
        "background_color": "vivid_blue",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "query_value",
              "title": "Requests from the public ingress straight to backends (sum over the timeframe)",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "autoscale": true,
              "precision": 0,
              "requests": [
                {
                  "response_format": "scalar",
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "d",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND source_workload:nginx-ingress-protected-controller AND NOT destination_workload:prod-ms-krakend-gateway}.as_count()",
                      "aggregator": "sum"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [
                    {
                      "formula": "d"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "query_value",
              "title": "Share of public traffic that goes through the gateway, %",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "autoscale": true,
              "precision": 1,
              "requests": [
                {
                  "response_format": "scalar",
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "g",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND source_workload:nginx-ingress-protected-controller AND destination_workload:prod-ms-krakend-gateway}.as_count()",
                      "aggregator": "sum"
                    },
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "d",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND source_workload:nginx-ingress-protected-controller AND NOT destination_workload:prod-ms-krakend-gateway}.as_count()",
                      "aggregator": "sum"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [
                    {
                      "formula": "g / (g + d) * 100"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "timeseries",
              "title": "Direct to backends vs through the gateway (per interval)",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "show_legend": true,
              "legend_layout": "auto",
              "legend_columns": [
                "avg",
                "max",
                "value"
              ],
              "requests": [
                {
                  "display_type": "line",
                  "response_format": "timeseries",
                  "style": {
                    "palette": "dog_classic",
                    "line_type": "solid",
                    "line_width": "normal"
                  },
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "direct",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND source_workload:nginx-ingress-protected-controller AND NOT destination_workload:prod-ms-krakend-gateway}.as_count()"
                    },
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "gateway",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND source_workload:nginx-ingress-protected-controller AND destination_workload:prod-ms-krakend-gateway}.as_count()"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [
                    {
                      "alias": "straight to backends",
                      "formula": "direct"
                    },
                    {
                      "alias": "through KrakenD",
                      "formula": "gateway"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "toplist",
              "title": "Backends still called from the public ingress (this list must shrink to the gateway only)",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "requests": [
                {
                  "response_format": "scalar",
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "q",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND source_workload:nginx-ingress-protected-controller} by {destination_workload}.as_count()",
                      "aggregator": "sum"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [
                    {
                      "formula": "q",
                      "limit": {
                        "count": 50,
                        "order": "desc"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "group",
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "show_title": true,
        "title": "Step A1 (SIT/UAT) and D1 (prod): Camunda engine REST API cluster-internal",
        "background_color": "vivid_orange",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "note",
              "content": "**What proves it.** After app-deployment 14179 merges in prod, the Istio sidecar of `prod-ms-bpm` answers **403** to the ingress controllers for `/bpm/engine-rest/*`; those 403s show below as a step up from today's baseline (the business API already returns about 400 403s an hour to the public ingress, measured 5 Oct 2026); the deny adds a 403 for every engine REST call that reaches the edge. Both controllers are denied: public (`nginx-ingress-protected-controller`) and VPN (`prod-nginx-ingres-private-controller`).\n\n**SIT and UAT (not visible here, app-deployment 14169):** `curl -sI https://microservices.sit.bravo.bfi.co.id/bpm/engine-rest/version` returns 403 (was 401); from a pod in the mesh the same path still returns 401; Cockpit `/bpm/camunda` and `/bpm/v1/**` unchanged. Then the same on UAT.",
              "background_color": "gray",
              "font_size": "14",
              "text_align": "left",
              "has_padding": true,
              "show_tick": false
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "timeseries",
              "title": "prod-ms-bpm: responses to the two ingress controllers, by code (403 = the deny firing)",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "show_legend": true,
              "legend_layout": "auto",
              "legend_columns": [
                "avg",
                "max",
                "value"
              ],
              "requests": [
                {
                  "display_type": "bars",
                  "response_format": "timeseries",
                  "style": {
                    "palette": "dog_classic",
                    "line_type": "solid",
                    "line_width": "normal"
                  },
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "r",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND destination_workload:prod-ms-bpm AND source_workload IN (nginx-ingress-protected-controller,prod-nginx-ingres-private-controller)} by {source_workload, response_code}.as_count()"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [
                    {
                      "formula": "r"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "query_value",
              "title": "403s from prod-ms-bpm to the ingress controllers (timeframe sum; baseline about 400 an hour before the deny)",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "autoscale": true,
              "precision": 0,
              "requests": [
                {
                  "response_format": "scalar",
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "r",
                      "query": "sum:istio.mesh.request.count.total{reporter:destination AND destination_workload:prod-ms-bpm AND source_workload IN (nginx-ingress-protected-controller,prod-nginx-ingres-private-controller) AND response_code:403}.as_count()",
                      "aggregator": "sum"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [
                    {
                      "formula": "r"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "group",
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "show_title": true,
        "title": "Steps A2, A3 (SIT/UAT) and D4 (prod): lora-schema hairpin, then public routes off",
        "background_color": "vivid_purple",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "note",
              "content": "**What proves it.** `prod-lora-schema` has no outside callers; its public traffic is LORA's own services going out through the public host and back in. After app-deployment 14181 (callers moved to the cluster-local address) the line from `nginx-ingress-protected-controller` must reach **zero within a day** and the lines from the LORA services must carry the same volume. Only then does 14178 (public Ingress off) merge; 14176 does the same for `lora-cdc-bridges` and `lora-diff-inspector`.\n\n**SIT and UAT (app-deployment 14180, then 14182):** no schema-fetch errors in the LORA workers, lora-task, cdc-bridges, bfi-connect and partnership for 24 h; then `curl -I https://microservices.sit.bravo.bfi.co.id/lora-schema/` returns 404 while the same path on `microservices-private.sit\u2026` over VPN still answers.",
              "background_color": "gray",
              "font_size": "14",
              "text_align": "left",
              "has_padding": true,
              "show_tick": false
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "timeseries",
              "title": "prod-lora-schema: requests by source (the ingress line must go to zero after 14181)",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "show_legend": true,
              "legend_layout": "auto",
              "legend_columns": [
                "avg",
