    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "group",
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "show_title": true,
        "title": "Steps B and D2: the gateway carries bpm and lora-task",
        "background_color": "vivid_green",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "note",
              "content": "**What proves it.** The two migration curves: requests to `prod-ms-bpm` and `prod-lora-task` split by source. As the consoles and the LORA back office switch to `gateway.prod\u2026`, the `nginx-ingress-protected-controller` line falls and the `prod-ms-krakend-gateway` line rises by the same amount. The gateway's own logs show the routed paths and their response codes, and the realtime plugin logs every proxied socket and stream (zero in prod until the prod lists are filled by the follow-up gateway PR and 14184 merges).\n\n**SIT and UAT (not visible here):** after the gateway tag with the plugin and app-deployment 14183: a WebSocket to `wss://gateway.sit.bravo.bfi.co.id/lora-task/messaging/ws/<task_id>` with a back-office session stays open past 60 s; `curl -N https://gateway.sit.bravo.bfi.co.id/lora-task/subscribe/tasks` streams past 60 s; `/lora-task/subscriber` returns 404; after the route PRs 417 and 419, `curl -sI https://gateway.sit.bravo.bfi.co.id/bpm/v1/users/me | head -1` shows 401, not 404.",
              "background_color": "gray",
              "font_size": "14",
              "text_align": "left",
              "has_padding": true,
              "show_tick": false
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "timeseries",
              "title": "prod-ms-bpm: requests by source (ingress falls, gateway rises)",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "show_legend": true,
              "legend_layout": "auto",
              "legend_columns": [
                "avg",
                "max",
                "value"
              ],
              "requests": [
